# The barrier the White Knight raises by shouting at what is in front of them.
# Cut when nothing read a monster debuff; enemy_attack_pct reads exactly that
# now -- it weakens the mob before its hit is rolled, so the character's DEF
# then cancels a larger share of what is left.
#
# GMS also takes the same share off the enemy's DEFENCE and its accuracy.
# Neither is modelled: a monster's DEF is a stat this game does not carry, and
# there is no accuracy to lose.
#
# Its success rate is dropped rather than folded in. GMS runs the debuff for
# 40 + 2L seconds off a cast the player can simply repeat until it lands, so
# what the rate costs is casts rather than damage -- and the debuff itself is
# permanent for the same reason every other rebuffable window here is.
#
# The six enemies it reaches say nothing either: only the mob at the front of
# the queue hits back.
name: "Noble Demand"
skill_order: 3
description:
  "Releases the pride of the Holy Knight, decreasing the Attack Power of "
  "nearby enemies."
kind: SKILL_KIND_PASSIVE
job_advancement: JOB_ADVANCEMENT_WHITE_KNIGHT
max_level: 20
base { enemy_attack_pct: 0.30 }
per_level { enemy_attack_pct: 0.01 }
